XR diorama: the HUD replay's partial clears transparent

Aurora draws partial EFB clears (an EFB copy with clear over less than the whole target) as a quad
in the clear colour. In the diorama's HUD replay (patch 0026) they painted the game's opaque clear
colour over the HUD's panel; they clear to transparent there, as its passes do.

diff --git a/lib/gfx/clear.cpp b/lib/gfx/clear.cpp
index 8b224f7..bf033e1 100644
--- a/lib/gfx/clear.cpp
+++ b/lib/gfx/clear.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #include "clear.hpp"
 
 #include "encoding.hpp"
+#include "stereo.hpp"
 #include "../webgpu/gpu.hpp"
 #include "tracy/Tracy.hpp"
 
@@ -143,7 +144,10 @@ void render(const DrawData& data, const wgpu::RenderPassEncoder& pass, const wgp
     return;
   }
 
-  pass.SetBlendConstant(&data.color);
+  // The diorama's HUD replay (patch 0028): its partial clears transparent too, as its passes' (0026);
+  // the game's clear colour painted the HUD's panel opaque black.
+  const wgpu::Color transparent{0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0};
+  pass.SetBlendConstant(stereo::hud_replay() ? &transparent : &data.color);
   pass.SetViewport(0.f, 0.f, static_cast<float>(targetSize.width), static_cast<float>(targetSize.height), data.depth,
                    data.depth);
   pass.SetScissorRect(data.rect.x, data.rect.y, data.rect.width, data.rect.height);
